-抛掉固体助推器
-分离轨道器。
-Jettison the SRB
-Jettison the orbiter.

400
00:19:32,067 --> 00:19:34,733
-然后操纵它滑翔降落。
-什么是轨道器？
-And fly it down.
-What's the orbiter?

401
00:19:34,767 --> 00:19:36,467
-用那辆雷利安特。
-行。
-The Reliant.
-Right.

402
00:19:36,500 --> 00:19:39,167
-不过你们手头有多余的
十亿美元吗？
-没有。
-Have you got a spare
billion dollars though?
-No.

403
00:19:39,200 --> 00:19:41,067
你看，
这就是我们来找你们的原因。
You see,
that why we've come to you.

404
00:19:41,100 --> 00:19:43,600
因为你们是曼彻斯特人，
肯定能花个十先令六便士
就给搞定。
Because you're form Manchester
and you'll be able to do it
for 10 and six.

405
00:19:43,633 --> 00:19:45,467
而且红茶管够，
想喝多少喝多少。
And there'll be as much tea
as you can drink.

406
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:50,433
梅：对，猪油炸薯条，
要啥有啥，
随便你们挑。
MAY: Yeah, chips in lard,
everything.
Anything you want.

407
00:19:50,467 --> 00:19:53,733
哈蒙德：这帮火箭专家
在笔记本电脑背面
草草算了算。
HAMMOND: The rocket men
did some calculations
on the back of a laptop.

408
00:19:54,700 --> 00:19:56,533
这该死的玩意儿
到底要怎么弄才能飞？
How do we make
this bloody thing work?

409
00:19:56,567 --> 00:19:57,767
（叹气）好吧，
好歹我们搞到了“知更鸟”。
(SIGHS) Well,
we've got the Robin.

410
00:19:57,800 --> 00:19:59,200
他们把“知更鸟”给咱了，
对吧。
They've given us Robin,
haven't they.

411
00:19:59,233 --> 00:20:01,533
-好歹是个起点。
-哇哦，好兴奋啊，真高兴。
-That's a starting point.
-Whoopee. Whoopee. Whoopee.

412
00:20:01,567 --> 00:20:03,700
我们有辆“知更鸟”了呢！
We've got a Robin!

413
00:20:03,733 --> 00:20:06,367
哈蒙德：一小时后，
事实证明杰里米
可能还真没说错。
HAMMOND: An hour later and
it looks as though Jeremy
might have had a point.

414
00:20:07,867 --> 00:20:11,800
这事儿方方面面
都难如登天。
It is difficult
in every single way.

415
00:20:12,233 --> 00:20:13,300
听着。
Right.

416
00:20:13,333 --> 00:20:15,067
你们挑了辆雷利安特·知更鸟，
You've got a Reliant Robin,

417
00:20:15,100 --> 00:20:18,400
-这是辆汽车，
所以它沉得要命。
-是的。
-it's a car
so it's really, really heavy.
-Yeah.

418
00:20:18,433 --> 00:20:20,233
粗略估算一下，
So rough numbers,

419
00:20:20,267 --> 00:20:23,667
我们需要的推力
大概是当年那辆Mini的
12倍左右……
we're gonna need about
12 times the amount of power
that the Mini had...

420
00:20:23,700 --> 00:20:25,300
真的假的？
Really?

421
00:20:25,333 --> 00:20:27,800
这将是欧洲发射过的
最大的一枚
非商业火箭。
It's the largest
non-commercial rocket
launched in Europe.

422
00:20:27,833 --> 00:20:32,767
这也将是欧洲发射过的
威力最强的
非商业火箭。
It's the most powerful
non-commercial rocket
launched in Europe.

423
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:34,567
行吧。
Right.

424
00:20:34,600 --> 00:20:37,600
单说作为火箭，
它的气动外形简直烂到
不能再烂了。
As a rocket,
it's the most awful shape
it could ever be.

425
00:20:37,633 --> 00:20:41,400
但我本来觉得选“知更鸟”
是个挺好的出发点，
因为……
But I thought the Robin
was a good place to start
because...

426
00:20:41,433 --> 00:20:43,667
它一头是尖的啊。
It's pointy at one end.

427
00:20:43,700 --> 00:20:45,567
我们当时也就
琢磨到这一步了。
That's as far
as we got with that.

428
00:20:45,600 --> 00:20:48,833
确实是尖的，得嘞，好吧。
It's pointy, shuck, yeah.

429
00:20:48,867 --> 00:20:52,867
哈蒙德：尽管如此，
他们还是带上詹姆斯
开工了。
HAMMOND: Nevertheless,
they set to work
with James in tow.

430
00:20:55,167 --> 00:20:58,967
当梅在这间全世界最大的
“菜园工具棚”里乐不思蜀时……
While May was in his element
in the world's biggest
allotment shed...

431
00:20:58,967 --> 00:21:00,467
哇！瞧瞧这个！
Aw! Look at that!

432
00:21:00,500 --> 00:21:04,200
我则在苦思冥想
到底该怎么让一辆雷利安特·知更鸟着陆。
I was trying to work out
how to land a Reliant Robin.

433
00:21:05,433 --> 00:21:07,767
如果火箭分离了……
If rockets are deployed...

434
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:11,067
就这样降落。
Land it like that.

435
00:21:11,100 --> 00:21:15,867
我苦苦纠结了老半天，
终于灵光一现。
I wrestled with the problem
for ages
before I had a brainwave.

436
00:21:15,967 --> 00:21:18,000
喂，您好。请问是
《航模月刊》吗？
Hello. Is that
Model Airplane monthly?

437
00:21:18,033 --> 00:21:20,733
太好了。我需要点帮助……
Great. I need some help...

438
00:21:29,833 --> 00:21:34,167
我觉得这就是终极答案，
只要换个动力更强劲的版本，
呃，不管这玩意儿叫什么，
This, I think, is the answer,
if in a more powerful version
well, of whatever this is,

439
00:21:34,200 --> 00:21:36,067
来当作我们的航天飞机。
to our space shuttle.

440
00:21:36,100 --> 00:21:39,400
等它抛掉火箭推进器之后，
我们就能在地面上
对它进行遥控操控。
Then we take control
of it from the ground after
it's jettisoned its rocket

441
00:21:39,433 --> 00:21:41,400
然后用遥控器开回来。
计划挺完美。
and fly it in by remote.
It's a good plan.

442
00:21:41,433 --> 00:21:43,733
就差把开飞机的技术练好了！
Just gotta get good at flying!

443
00:21:47,433 --> 00:21:50,533
我觉得最好还是
把自己从这个岗位上开除，
I thought it best
to sack myself from this job

444
00:21:50,567 --> 00:21:53,000
转而雇了
史蒂夫·霍兰德，
and instead hired
Steve Holland,

445
00:21:53,033 --> 00:21:56,000
一位航模飞行
全国冠军。
a champion
model aeroplane pilot.

446
00:21:56,033 --> 00:21:59,100
对喽，
这才像样嘛，
史蒂夫。
Yeah,
now that is more like it,
Steve.

447
00:22:02,467 --> 00:22:05,500
你开“飞车”技术怎么样？
How are you at flying cars?

448
00:22:05,533 --> 00:22:07,833
-车？
-小车。
-Cars?
-Small cars.

449
00:22:07,867 --> 00:22:11,833
搞定了飞行员史蒂夫，
我回去视察
詹姆斯的组装进度，
With Steve the pilot on board,
I went back to check
on James' build,

450
00:22:11,867 --> 00:22:14,200
结果当场被吓傻了。
and I was in for a shock.

451
00:22:15,633 --> 00:22:18,033
我的天哪，詹姆斯！
（难以置信地笑）
Bloody hell, James!
(LAUGHS DISBELIEVINGLY)

452
00:22:18,067 --> 00:22:19,467
这也太巨大了吧！
It's enormous!

453
00:22:19,500 --> 00:22:22,600
那是固体火箭助推器，
总共有两个。
That's a solid rocket booster,
there are two of those.

454
00:22:22,633 --> 00:22:24,600
那个甚至还没装上
整流罩锥头呢。
That hasn't even got
its nose cone on yet.

455
00:22:24,633 --> 00:22:26,033
实际上比这还要大一号。
It's actually a bit bigger
than that.

456
00:22:26,067 --> 00:22:28,300
可这也……
我还以为就是在木棍上
插个大窜天猴呢。
But it's...
I was thinking
firework on a stick.

457
00:22:28,333 --> 00:22:30,000
我知道，我原本也这么想。
I know. So was I.

458
00:22:30,033 --> 00:22:32,500
但这还不是
最大的部件。
But that isn't
the biggest bit.

459
00:22:32,533 --> 00:22:35,533
梅：
没错，外挂燃料箱才是最大的大头，
MAY:
No, the external fuel tank
was the biggest bit,

460
00:22:35,567 --> 00:22:38,067
底部还配有额外的火箭引擎，
complete with extra rockets
in the bottom

461
00:22:38,100 --> 00:22:40,200
然后那辆烈羚（Reliant）里也塞了更多火箭，
then there were more rockets
in the Reliant,

462
00:22:40,233 --> 00:22:42,967
还有用于分离各个级段的爆炸螺栓。
and explosive bolts
to separate everything.

463
00:22:42,967 --> 00:22:47,100
整个机械结构复杂得
令人匪夷所思。
The whole construction
was mind-bogglingly
complicated.

464
00:22:47,133 --> 00:22:51,633
我现在突然意识到，
可能出幺蛾子的环节……
What occurs to me now
is the list of things
to go wrong...

465
00:22:51,667 --> 00:22:53,967
-多如牛毛。
-没错。
-Is enormous.
-Yeah.

466
00:22:53,967 --> 00:22:55,833
而且只要其中任何一个出了岔子……
And if any one of them
goes wrong...

467
00:22:55,867 --> 00:22:58,400
你看，我之前一直还在操心着陆的事。
See, I've been worried
about the landing.

468
00:22:58,433 --> 00:23:02,633
到了发射那天，能顺顺当当
撑到着陆阶段的几率，
现在看来……
The chances of getting as far
as the landing on the day,
are now...

469
00:23:02,667 --> 00:23:05,433
-顺便问下，你飞机练得
怎么样了？
-挺好。
-How did you get on
with your flying, by the way?
-Good.

470
00:23:08,967 --> 00:23:11,000
下一个问题可就棘手了。
The next problem was a biggie.

471
00:23:11,033 --> 00:23:14,400
火箭专家们担心，
由于罗宾那奇葩的外形，
The rocketeers were worried
that because of
the Robin's odd shape,

472
00:23:14,433 --> 00:23:18,467
整架航天飞机在爬升过程中
会直接一头扎偏航线。
the whole shuttle
would spear off course
during the ascent.

473
00:23:18,500 --> 00:23:20,967
所以，推力足够这点我们不用担心。
So, we're happy
we've got the power.

474
00:23:20,967 --> 00:23:22,967
是啊，足足八吨推力。
Yeah, eight tonnes of thrust.

475
00:23:22,967 --> 00:23:27,000
而这破玩意儿才一吨半重，
所以肯定能窜上天。
And the thing only weighs
one-and-a-half
so it's gonna go somewhere.

476
00:23:27,033 --> 00:23:29,367
这绝对要搞砸的，对吧？
（笑）
It's not going to work, is it?
(LAUGHS)

477
00:23:29,400 --> 00:23:32,967
-行了，必须搞成，
咱们都已经陷这么深了。
-那是什么？
-Well, it's got to work.
We're a long way into it now.
-What's that?

478
00:23:32,967 --> 00:23:35,600
我知道，但要是
从这个角度看，
就合理多了。
Yeah, I know, but
if you look at it like this
it makes a lot more sense.

479
00:23:35,633 --> 00:23:38,300
-（大笑）
-梅，我们必须保证
它不只是光能射上去。
-(LAUGHING)
-May, we've got to make sure
it doesn't just launch.

480
00:23:38,333 --> 00:23:39,700
我的意思是比如……
I mean like...

481
00:23:39,733 --> 00:23:41,967
它在天上可能会直接仰面翻过去什么的。
It could fall onto its back
in the sky or anything.

482
00:23:41,967 --> 00:23:43,733
现在这已经不是动力的问题了。
This isn't about power now.

483
00:23:43,767 --> 00:23:47,700
而是它的外形，以及这会如何
影响它的飞行轨迹。
This is about the shape of it
and how that will affect
where it goes.

484
00:23:47,733 --> 00:23:49,167
它的轨迹。
这是空气动力学问题。
Where it goes.
It's aerodynamic.

485
00:23:49,200 --> 00:23:52,067
我们得找个空气动力学专家
来看看这堆玩意儿。
We need an aerodynamics expert
to look at all this stuff.

486
00:23:54,067 --> 00:23:58,067
哈蒙德：一通低声下气的求人电话
打到了西英格兰大学，
HAMMOND: One grovelling
phone call to the University
of the West of England,

487
00:23:58,100 --> 00:24:01,267
我们总算搞到了
使用他们风洞的许可。
and we secured permission
to use their wind tunnel.

488
00:24:01,300 --> 00:24:05,833
而且既然是免费的，
我们就理所当然地以为
这地方是全自助的。
And because it was free,
we assumed
it was self-service.

489
00:24:05,867 --> 00:24:08,300
-开始！
-等等，什么叫“开始”？
我都不知道该……
-Go!
-Well, what do you mean, "Go"?
I don't know what...

490
00:24:09,200 --> 00:24:10,200
呃……
Uh...

491
00:24:17,833 --> 00:24:19,200
就摆那个姿势！
Do that!

492
00:24:21,367 --> 00:24:22,633
很好！
That's good!

493
00:24:22,667 --> 00:24:24,533
但无论他怎么拼命折腾，
No matter how hard he tried,

494
00:24:24,567 --> 00:24:27,700
詹姆斯都没法把自己
摆成一辆Reliant Robin的形状，
James couldn't make himself
into the shape
of a Reliant Robin,

495
00:24:27,733 --> 00:24:28,967
就算有人搭手也不行。
even with help.

496
00:24:31,333 --> 00:24:33,200
谢天谢地，
两位技术宅专家终于赶到了，
Thankfully,
two eggheads arrived

497
00:24:33,233 --> 00:24:35,433
还带来了我们航天飞机的缩比模型。
with the scale model
of our shuttle.

498
00:24:35,467 --> 00:24:39,100
只要看到这种大胡子，你就知道
绝对稳了，专业靠谱。
You see a beard like that
and you know
you're in safe hands.

499
00:24:39,133 --> 00:24:40,500
梅：没错。
MAY: Yup.

500
00:24:40,533 --> 00:24:42,200
（机器轰鸣声）
(MACHINE WHIRRING)

501
00:24:44,433 --> 00:24:48,767
基本上，我们是在排查任何
空气动力学上的恶心隐患。
Well, basically,
we're looking for anything
aerodynamically nasty.

502
00:24:48,800 --> 00:24:51,167
没错，这台Reliant在气动上就是个灾难。
Yeah, the Reliant is a problem
aerodynamically.

503
00:24:51,200 --> 00:24:54,433
哈蒙德：好吧，
人家造这车时本来也没指望它上天，对吧？
HAMMOND: Well,
they didn't really design it
with this in mind, did they?

504
00:24:54,467 --> 00:24:56,967
机翼上有做几何扭转
或者气动扭转吗？
Is there any wash-out
or wash-in on the wings?

505
00:24:56,967 --> 00:25:01,100
基本上就是非常简单的……
对称翼型。
Basically it's simple...
symmetrical aerofoils.

506
00:25:01,133 --> 00:25:03,833
哈蒙德：我完全听不懂
你们俩在说什么鬼话。
HAMMOND: I don't know
what you two are saying.

507
00:25:03,867 --> 00:25:06,267
-这个嘛，机翼有个翼型剖面……
-呃……（傻眼）
-Well, there is the aerofoil
section of the wing...
-Duh...

508
00:25:07,100 --> 00:25:08,167
行吧。
Right.

509
00:25:08,800 --> 00:25:10,833
那么，终极问题来了，
So, the big question,

510
00:25:11,667 --> 00:25:12,967
它能飞起来吗？
will it fly?

511
00:25:15,433 --> 00:25:18,767
从他的沉默中我看得出来，
他心里直犯嘀咕。
I took it from his silence
that he had his doubts.

512
00:25:20,433 --> 00:25:22,467
而且不止他一个人这么想。
And he wasn't alone.

513
00:25:22,500 --> 00:25:25,700
和真正的航天飞机一样，
我们的穿梭机也要无动力滑翔返航。
Like the real thing,
our shuttle would glide
back to earth without power.

514
00:25:25,733 --> 00:25:31,100
我们的试飞员史蒂夫也做了一个模型，
来演示它滑翔的效果到底如何。
And Steve, our pilot,
had also built a model
to show how well it did this.

515
00:25:31,133 --> 00:25:33,433
你觉得这玩意儿
飞起来究竟会是什么感觉？
What is it actually
going to feel like to fly,
do you think?

516
00:25:33,467 --> 00:25:36,800
呃，下坠的感觉大概就像
钢缆被切断的电梯。
Well, it's gonna
come down like a lift
with the cable cut.

517
00:25:36,833 --> 00:25:38,733
史蒂夫，你这话可一点都没给我希望啊。
You're not filling me
with hope, Steve.

518
00:25:38,767 --> 00:25:42,233
呃，大多数普通飞机，
它们滑翔时大概是这样，你知道的，
Well, most normal aeroplanes,
they sort of glide
for about, you know,

519
00:25:42,267 --> 00:25:45,967
向前滑翔二十英尺，
高度大概只下降一英尺。
they fly 20 feet forward,
they lose about
a foot in height.

520
00:25:45,967 --> 00:25:47,200
对。
Yeah.

521
00:25:47,233 --> 00:25:48,767
恐怕罗宾的方向装反了。
I'm afraid the Robin
is the other way round.

522
00:25:52,300 --> 00:25:54,467
三、二、一……
Three, two, one...

523
00:25:54,500 --> 00:25:58,233
哈蒙德：当模型脱离了
牵引机之后……
HAMMOND: And when the model
was released
from its tow plane...

524
00:25:58,267 --> 00:26:00,767
它直接冲着地球一头栽下去了！
It's just plummeting
to the Earth!

525
00:26:06,867 --> 00:26:09,600
跟你说，换你上去我可不奉陪！
I'd rather you than me,
I tell you!

526
00:26:09,633 --> 00:26:12,633
所以，我们的航天飞机能不能飞上天，
还得打个问号。
So, there were doubts about
our space shuttle going up.

527
00:26:12,667 --> 00:26:15,167
能不能落得回来，
也是个未知数。
And doubts about it
coming down.

528
00:26:15,200 --> 00:26:18,100
但现在操心已经太迟了，
因为这个大宝贝已经准备就绪，
But it was too late
to worry now
because she was ready

529
00:26:18,133 --> 00:26:20,967
正运往发射场。
and on her way
to the launch site.

530
00:26:24,367 --> 00:26:27,833
（观众欢呼）
(AUDIENCE CHEERING)

531
00:26:27,867 --> 00:26:31,067
别担心，
我保证我依然热爱汽车！
Don't worry,
I still like cars, I promise!

532
00:26:31,100 --> 00:26:35,000
